From 89a85296ea0cb7c56ef50fd0e3b11a1614a615de Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 01:48:27 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] feat(edm): wire no-core burnout - a pocket burnt out by
 offset rings, no core left

A Wire Contour with a burnout clearance burns a closed pocket's whole
interior out: offset rings from the stated wall clearance inward, 0.9 x
the kerf offset apart, cut innermost first from one threading at the
start hole. A clearance below the kerf offset, a missing or misplaced
start hole, the punch side and a pattern that splits into islands are
refused by name; the no-core law (kerf swept out of the pocket, every
piece left must be the wall's) refuses a core. #534's slug law reads a
burnout as "must free nothing" (WireFinding::Core), and its kerf law
blocks a ring that gouges a wall. The field rides the file mirror
(burnout_clearance), and so the MCP params door; absent, every existing
document, stamp and golden is unchanged.

Fixes #540

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
